WEBVTT

00:04:58.881 --> 00:05:02.097
2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 2.

00:05:02.097 --> 00:05:05.501
So 2 ^ 5 is 2 x 2 = 4,

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.681
8, 16, 32.

00:05:07.681 --> 00:05:11.195
If you've got that, you're with me for the entire journey. Okay?

00:05:11.195 --> 00:05:13.167
So 2 ^ 5,

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:14.879
those five little twos multiplied together.

00:05:14.879 --> 00:05:19.142
(2 ^ 5) - 1 = 31.

00:05:19.142 --> 00:05:22.453
31 is a prime number, and that five in the power

00:05:22.453 --> 00:05:24.998
is also a prime number.

00:05:24.998 --> 00:05:28.502
And the vast bulk of massive primes we've ever found

00:05:28.502 --> 00:05:29.738
are of that form:

00:05:29.738 --> 00:05:33.017
two to a prime number, take away one.